      "worked": "Natalie paints 1 house in 4 days, so she paints 5 houses in 20 days.\n\nErin paints 1 house in 5 days, so she paints 4 houses in 20 days.\n\nTogether they paint $5+4=9$ houses in 20 days.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Time for one house}&=20\\div9\\text{ days}\\\\\\text{Time for one house}&=\\frac{20}{9}\\text{ days}\\\\\\text{Time for one house}&=2\\frac{2}{9}\\text{ days}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
